{
  "$comment": "The static half of the action registry (docs/adr/0041-registre-d-actions-menus-et-raccourcis.md, point 1). Read by registry.ts in the front and by crates/oxyn-desktop/src/menu.rs through include_str!: moving this file breaks the Rust build, which is the point. Nothing here is executable. Shortcuts: `Mod` is ⌘ on macOS and Ctrl elsewhere; `Ctrl` is the Control key on every platform. `binding`: `dispatcher` (default) is bound by lib/actions/keyboard.ts or by the native macOS menu; `component` is handled by the component of its zone and only shown; `system` is the webview's own editing key, only shown. A menu's `roles` are the macOS system items (Edit's Copy, Hide…), placed by group and order among the actions; the web bar of Windows and Linux ignores them.",
